course: dictionary
lesson: 8594
title: One word, many meanings: score
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Score is one of them. Read the sentence around it to find which meaning fits. «Wee Callum said he'd scored a hat-trick, and Dad was so chuffed.» Chuffed means pleased, and a hat-trick is three goals in one game, so scored must mean got goals in a game.
explain: In school, a score is a mark in a test or the points in a game. «Teachers are pleased by a score of 100%.» Here score means the mark you get. Ask yourself: is this a game, a test, or something else? The clues tell you which meaning to use.
explain: Score also has meanings that are less common. «Tadhg scores and Cian says, Not bad, ya sap.» Here scores means gets a point or goal. Sap is Irish slang for a softie or a fool, said fondly here. Try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right one.
fact: A score is the number of points, goals or marks someone gets in a game or test.
fact: To score means to get a point, a goal or a mark.
fact: A score is also the written music for a band, an orchestra or a film.
fact: Four score is an old way of saying 80, because a score means 20 things.
fact: To score a line means to scratch or cut it into a surface.
exercise: «Wee Callum said he'd scored a hat-trick, and Dad was so chuffed.» What does scored mean here? | *Got goals in a game | Lost the game badly | Cut a line into a wall | Wrote a song for a band
exercise: «Teachers are pleased by a score of 100%.» What is a score of 100% in a test? | A perfect mark | *A perfect mark, the best possible result in a test | The number of players in a team | The lowest mark you can get
exercise: In an old story, «four score» means what number? | 4 | 20 | 40 | *80
test: «What's the score?» asks someone how the game stands. | Who is the best player | What time it is | How much a ticket costs | *How the game stands
test: «To settle a score» means to | *Get back at someone | Write music for a film | Win a prize for reading | Count to twenty
exam: «The band played the score from the film.» Here score means | *Written music | A line scratched on a surface | Points in a game | A test mark
